@startuml state-iter4
title Reservation Lifecycle — Cumulative through Iteration 4 (State pattern)\n(no new states in iter4; red = transition newly driven by iter4 admin refund-review queue)
hide empty description
skinparam stateFontSize 12
skinparam ranksep 48
skinparam nodesep 32
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130

[*] -down-> Initiated
Initiated -right-> PendingPayment : processPayment()
PendingPayment -right-> Confirmed : payment authorized
PendingPayment -down-> Cancelled : handlePaymentFailure()
Confirmed -right-> Ticketed : issueTicket()
Confirmed -down-> CancellationRequested : requestCancellation()
Ticketed -down-> CancellationRequested : requestCancellation()
CancellationRequested -left-> Cancelled : confirmCancellation()
Cancelled -down-> RefundRequested : requestRefund()
RefundRequested -[#CC0000]-> Refunded : processRefundDecision()\n(iter4: admin review queue)
Refunded -right-> [*]

note right of RefundRequested #FFF0F0
  <b><color:#CC0000>Iteration 4 change</color></b>
  RefundRequested -> Refunded is now driven by
  the admin refund-review queue (RefundHandler:
  evaluateRefund -> processRefund). The state set
  itself is unchanged from iter3 — the 6 iter4
  patterns are orthogonal to this lifecycle.
end note

note left of PendingPayment
  iter3 (Observer): PendingPayment -> Cancelled
  also triggered by AutoCancelListener on
  PaymentFailedEvent / SeatHoldExpiredEvent.
end note
@enduml
